<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<RootNamespace>DotGram.Finance</RootNamespace>
		<Description>FIX 4.2, 4.4 and 5.0 SP2 tag-value parsing and validation: the wire read by a DotGram grammar, and each version's typed messages and checks generated from the FIX repository.</Description>

		<PackageReleaseNotes>Since 0.2.0. Validation is a question that keeps nothing, every finding says its way through the groups, the limits are the context's, and the types the reader builds are closed to code outside the package. The README has the whole surface; what follows is what changed and what to write instead.

BREAKING CHANGES, and what to write instead

- Validate keeps nothing. message.Validate(context) returns an IReadOnlyList&lt;FixFinding&gt;, empty when nothing is wrong and new on every call; InvalidFindings and IsValid are gone, and a second Validate asks again of the context it is given (it used to answer what the first call found). `if (!message.Validate(context)) Report(message.InvalidFindings)` -&gt; `var findings = message.Validate(context); if (findings.Count &gt; 0) Report(findings);`. Validate(context, findings) adds to a collection of the caller's and returns how many it added. What reading found is message.Findings, read-only and never null.
- FixFinding is a sealed class made by its factories: new FixFinding(rule, tag, position, field, entryIndex) -&gt; FixFinding.Missing(tag), FixFinding.Of(rule, field) or FixFinding.Of(rule, tag), each with the path after it. EntryIndex -&gt; Path, every group and entry on the way to the finding, outermost first, each a FixGroupStep(CounterTag, Index); a finding prints it (453[1].802[0] tag 803 at 86: DuplicateField). Position is -1 for a field the message does not have, where it was 0. Two findings are the same only if they are one object.
- A custom message: OnValidate(context) -&gt; OnValidate(context, findings), adding to the collection it is given. FixCustomMessage.AddFinding may be called only from Place, on the thread that reads the message; anywhere else it throws InvalidOperationException. FixMessage.AddFinding, SetStandardField and the setters of the standard header's and trailer's properties are the package's own.
- FixMessage.Invalid -&gt; FixMessage.Unknown, the message of a MsgType nothing builds; its finding is UnknownMessageType.
- A group entry is built by the reader alone: the 644 entry classes lose their public constructor, and the entry's first field is a get-only property that is never null.
- FixField, the typed field classes under it and FixContext cannot be derived from outside the package.
- The limits are the context's. The largest message read from a reader or a stream is the context's MaxMessageLength (16 MiB unless given); the maxMessageLength parameter of ReadMessage, TryReadMessage, ReadMessages and ParseMessages and FixParser.DefaultMaxMessageLength are gone: ReadMessage(input, maxMessageLength: n) -&gt; ReadMessage(input, context with { MaxMessageLength = n }). Fix44Context.WithLogFraming -&gt; Fix44Context.Log, one shared value (likewise Fix42Context and Fix50Context). FixMessageFactory -&gt; MessageFactory. The emitTo parameter of With, Load and LoadFile is gone: Load(text, directory) -&gt; (context with { CheckSourceDirectory = directory }).Load(text). A Framing that is neither Wire nor Log throws ArgumentOutOfRangeException when it is set.
- FixDictionaryField takes its tag in its constructor, and applying a dictionary refuses a field stored under a key other than its tag.
- A null argument throws ArgumentNullException from every Try call; TryParseMessage of a null byte array used to answer false.

CHANGED

- A coded field whose text does not read as its type (Side 54=XYZ) is an InvalidValue finding; Validate used to throw InvalidOperationException from its Value.
- Every finding inside a group carries its path, and a finding of the whole message about a field inside an entry (a length not followed by its data, an encoded field without MessageEncoding) carries that entry's.
- The Try calls are annotated for nullability: after true the message is not null, after false the error is not null.
- BuildMessage reads a log with padded separators when the context frames a log; TryBuildMessage is public; both take the octets as a ReadOnlyMemory&lt;byte&gt; as well as a string.
- A stream reads a BeginString of any length and accepts another version's BeginString as a buffer does; Validate reports it.
- A tag nothing defines keeps its text in FixField.Invalid.RawText, or its octets in RawBytes.

FASTER

- A message with groups reads 5-10% faster, and large messages up to 11% (FIX 5.0 reports), with the same allocation: the reader stores every member in a field behind a get-only property. The assembly and the generated sources are smaller.
- A long data field read from a string is narrowed with a vectorized path on .NET.

KNOWN ISSUES

- A stream cannot read a log padded with spaces (read it whole), and a BodyLength that is missing or malformed ends the stream with a diagnostic, since without it there is no telling where the message ends.</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageTags>fix;finance;trading;parser;dotgram</PackageTags>

		<!-- The package ships its XML documentation, and every public member has some:
		     under TreatWarningsAsErrors a member left undocumented fails the build. -->
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

		<DebugType>embedded</DebugType>
		<ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
		<EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles>true</EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles>
		<CompilerGeneratedFilesOutputPath>$(BaseIntermediateOutputPath)GeneratedFiles</CompilerGeneratedFilesOutputPath>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="DotGram.Finance.Tests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="DotGram.Handwritten" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="DotGram.Finance.Fix44" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="DotGram.Finance.Fix44.Tests" />

		<!-- The benchmarks read the composed rule text and compile it, which needs the tables and
		     the nodes the text is written against. Nothing ships from that project. -->
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="DotGram.Finance.Benchmarks" />

		<ProjectReference Include="../DotGram/DotGram.csproj" OutputItemType="Analyzer" ReferenceOutputAssembly="false" />

		<!-- The generator's own output, analysed for dead or redundant emitted code
		     (tools/DotGram.GeneratedAnalyzers), never packed, loaded only under
		     DotGramAnalyzeGenerated=true (docs/development.md). -->
		<ProjectReference Include="../../tools/DotGram.GeneratedAnalyzers/DotGram.GeneratedAnalyzers.csproj"
		                  OutputItemType="Analyzer" ReferenceOutputAssembly="false"
		                  Condition="'$(DotGramAnalyzeGenerated)' == 'true'" />

		<!-- A dictionary loaded at run time is turned into the same straight-line checks the package
		     compiles in, written as text and compiled by the expression language: one lambda a
		     slot, typed on the class it checks. -->
		<ProjectReference Include="../DotGram.ExpressionLanguage/DotGram.ExpressionLanguage.csproj" />

		<!-- The public surface, held to PublicAPI.*.txt beside this file. What only one framework
		     has is in PublicAPI/<framework>/: a record's clone returns its own type on net10.0 and
		     the base type on netstandard2.0, which has no covariant returns. -->
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers" PrivateAssets="all" />
		<AdditionalFiles Include="PublicAPI/$(TargetFramework)/PublicAPI.*.txt" />

		<AdditionalFiles Include="Fix/**/*.gram" />

		<!-- The generator is a file-based app (top-level statements, run with `dotnet run`), not part
		     of this package: the default globbing above would otherwise compile it into the project. -->
		<Compile Remove="Fix/generate.cs" />

		<None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />

		<!-- The skill beside it, so that an agent working in a project that has restored
		     this package can read how to use it without leaving the machine. The README
		     says where it is, in a comment nothing renders. -->
		<None Include="SKILL.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />

		<!-- The FIX reference, packed beside the fields and messages it documents, so an agent
		     reading the restored package offline has it without a repository to browse. -->
		<None Include="Fix/README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="Fix/" />

		<None Include="../../LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="licenses/DotGram/" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="System.Memory" />
		<PackageReference Include="Portable.System.DateTimeOnly" />
		<PackageReference Include="Meziantou.Polyfill" PrivateAssets="all" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
